<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE suite SYSTEM "http://testng.org/testng-1.0.dtd">
<suite name="ogcapi-connectedsystems10-${version}" verbose="0" configfailurepolicy="continue">
  <parameter name="iut"  value=""/>
  <parameter name="auth-credential"  value=""/>
  <parameter name="mutation-tests-enabled"  value=""/>
  <parameter name="mutation-iut-policy"  value=""/>
  <parameter name="mobile-system-id"  value=""/>
  <parameter name="subdeployment-association-evidence"  value=""/>

  <listeners>
    <listener class-name="org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.listener.TestRunListener" />
    <listener class-name="org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.listener.SuiteFixtureListener" />
    <listener class-name="org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.listener.TestFailureListener" />
  </listeners>

  <!-- Single <test> block hosts Core, SystemFeatures, AND Common classes so TestNG's
       group-dependency mechanism resolves group "core" within the same scope as
       the "systemfeatures" group (group dependencies are <test>-scoped — methods
       in different <test> blocks cannot reference each other's groups, per
       TestNG-1.0.dtd semantics; verified empirically via DependencyMap "depends
       on nonexistent group" error when split across blocks).

       Group "part1apicommon" depends-on "core common", and "systemfeatures"
       depends-on "part1apicommon", so all systemfeatures-tagged @Tests SKIP
       gracefully if a released prerequisite is not satisfied (closes
       SCENARIO-ETS-PART1-002-SYSTEMFEATURES-DEPENDENCY-SKIP-001 per design.md
       §"SystemFeatures conformance class scope" snippet).

       Group "common" is INDEPENDENT of Core (same group-dependency-DAG-root level
       — see architect-handoff S-ETS-03-07 readiness rationale + Sprint 3 contract
       acceptance criterion). Common runs in parallel with Core; the load-bearing
       Common assertions are at the JSON-encoding-class layer + Common Part 2
       collections layer which Core does NOT cover (Core asserts the
       landing-page+oas30 SUCCESS-side sub-requirements only). Sprint 4+ may
       reconsider when 4+ classes need the BeforeSuite SkipException pattern noted
       in Sprint 2 inline comment.

       <run> block has no <include>/<exclude> filter so all groups run; the
       dependency map handles ordering and skip semantics.
       Core tests stay in group "core"; SystemFeatures tests stay in group
       "systemfeatures"; Common tests stay in group "common". -->
  <!-- Sprint 46 S-ETS-46-01 (REQ-ETS-PART1-001): the released OGC 23-001
       /conf/api-common class is distinct from inherited OGC API Common.
       part1apicommon depends on core+common; SystemFeatures now depends on
       part1apicommon and all existing descendants inherit that prerequisite. -->
  <!-- Sprint 48 S-ETS-48-01 (REQ-ETS-PART1-003): Subsystems retains its
       two-level dependency chain (Subsystems to SystemFeatures to API Common/Core)
       while replacing the historical four-method approximation. The @BeforeClass
       gate loads only immutable arguments and blocks failed or unexpected skipped
       prerequisites. Each of the five released direct procedures independently
       retrieves its own hierarchy, media, or association evidence, so one
       procedure's no-data SKIP cannot suppress unrelated methods. -->
  <!-- Sprint 49 S-ETS-49-01 (REQ-ETS-PART1-004): Deployments now implements
       the five released procedures and depends directly on API Common. Sprint 50
       likewise moves Procedures from its historical SystemFeatures dependency to
       direct API Common inheritance. Both setup gates filter prerequisite results
       to Core, Common, and API Common so sibling configuration outcomes cannot
       suppress their direct procedures. -->
  <!-- Sprint 52 S-ETS-52-01 (REQ-ETS-PART1-007): Sampling Features replaces
       its historical four-method approximation with exactly five independent
       released procedures. It inherits System, whose API Common and Core/Common
       prerequisites remain transitive. Its alwaysRun setup performs a defensive,
       class-filtered prerequisite gate so unrelated sibling configuration results
       cannot suppress direct Sampling Features evidence. Property Definitions
       retains its existing System dependency. -->
  <!-- Sprint 51 S-ETS-51-01 (REQ-ETS-PART1-005): exactly five independent
       released Subdeployment procedures depend directly on Deployment.
       API Common and Core/Common remain transitive prerequisites. -->
  <!-- Sprint 54 S-ETS-54-01 (REQ-ETS-PART1-012): GeoJSON implements the twelve
       released Annex A procedures. The class inherits /conf/api-common directly;
       resource-specific declarations and evidence are independently gated at runtime. -->
  <!-- Sprint 10 S-ETS-10-01 (REQ-ETS-PART1-013): SensorML group added as a PARTIAL
       systems read-only subset. SensorML depends-on="systemfeatures" because the subset
       validates system SensorML representations and must cascade-SKIP if SystemFeatures
       fails. This sprint intentionally leaves mediatype-write, relation-types,
       deployment/procedure/property schema/mapping, and full SensorML 3.0 schema
       validation open. -->
  <!-- Sprint 55 S-ETS-55-01 (REQ-ETS-PART1-009): Advanced Filtering implements
       exactly the 25 released Annex A procedures and inherits /conf/api-common
       directly. Every alwaysRun procedure independently reacquires declaration,
       seed, filtered, association, pagination, and representation evidence. -->
  <!-- Historical Sprint 12 S-ETS-12-01 (REQ-ETS-PART1-010), superseded by
       Sprint 56: CreateReplaceDelete was added as a systems-only safety-gated
       subset and then depended on
       "systemfeatures" because it validates /systems mutation behavior and must
       cascade-SKIP if SystemFeatures fails. POST/PUT/DELETE are guarded by explicit
       mutation-tests-enabled=true plus mutation-iut-policy=dedicated-mutable-iut; the
       known public GeoRobotix IUT is hard-denied even if both parameters are set. -->
  <!-- Sprint 57 S-ETS-57-01 (REQ-ETS-PART1-011): Update implements the five
       released Annex A procedures. Annex A directly inherits Part 1 API Common;
       Create/Replace/Delete supplies owned fixtures but is not a sibling TestNG
       prerequisite. Every procedure independently gates exact declarations,
       mutation ownership, PATCH negotiation, postconditions, and cleanup. -->
  <!-- Sprint 59 S-ETS-59-01 (REQ-ETS-PART2-001): Part 2 API Common closes the two
       released Annex A procedures and depends directly on "part1apicommon" because
       OGC 23-002 /req/api-common inherits OGC 23-001 /req/api-common. Missing Part 2
       /conf/api-common remains a runtime SKIP inside each direct procedure. -->
  <!-- Sprint 60 S-ETS-60-01 (REQ-ETS-PART2-002): Part 2 Datastream now implements
       the fourteen released Annex A procedures exactly. It inherits Part 2 API
       Common directly because OGC 23-002 /req/datastream lists /req/api-common as
       a prerequisite; every direct procedure remains independently runtime-gated
       for the Datastream declaration and conditional resource evidence. -->
  <!-- Sprint 61 S-ETS-61-01 (REQ-ETS-PART2-003): Part 2 ControlStream now
       implements the eighteen released Annex A procedures exactly. It inherits
       Part 2 API Common directly because OGC 23-002 /req/controlstream lists
       /req/api-common as a prerequisite; every direct procedure remains
       independently runtime-gated for the ControlStream declaration and
       conditional resource evidence. -->
  <!-- Sprint 62 S-ETS-62-01 (REQ-ETS-PART2-004): Part 2 Feasibility now implements
       the five released Annex A procedures exactly. It inherits ControlStream
       directly because OGC 23-002 /req/feasibility lists /req/controlstream as
       a prerequisite; every direct procedure remains runtime-gated for the
       Feasibility declaration and no IUT-bound feasibility mutation is issued. -->
  <!-- Sprint 63 S-ETS-63-01 (REQ-ETS-PART2-005): Part 2 System Events now implements
       the five released Annex A procedures exactly. It inherits Part 2 API Common and
       Part 1 System directly because OGC 23-002 /req/system-event lists /req/api-common
       and Part 1 /req/system as prerequisites; every direct procedure remains
       runtime-gated for the System Events declaration and no streaming or mutation
       request is issued. -->
  <!-- Sprint 64 S-ETS-64-01 (REQ-ETS-PART2-006): Part 2 Advanced Filtering now
       implements the eighteen released Annex A procedures exactly. It inherits
       Part 2 API Common and Part 1 Advanced Filtering directly because OGC 23-002
       /req/advanced-filtering lists both as prerequisites; resource-specific
       conformance classes remain runtime gates inside each direct procedure. -->
  <!-- Sprint 26 S-ETS-26-01 (REQ-ETS-PART2-007): Part 2 Create/Replace/Delete group
       added as a safety-gated subset. It depends on "core common systemfeatures" so
       foundational resources are available, but not on Part2ApiCommon or Part 2
       resource-class groups; runtime checks keep prerequisite honesty, OPTIONS-only
       readiness, unavailable endpoints, and public-IUT mutation denial visible. -->
  <!-- Sprint 27 S-ETS-27-01 (REQ-ETS-PART2-008): Part 2 Update group added as a
       safety-gated PATCH subset. It depends on "core common systemfeatures" so
       foundational resources are available, but not on Part2ApiCommon, Part 1 Update,
       Part 2 Create/Replace/Delete, or resource-class groups; runtime checks keep
       CRD/Features4 prerequisites, Clause 15 condition gates, OPTIONS PATCH readiness,
       unavailable endpoints, schema-rejection honesty, and public-IUT mutation denial
       visible. -->
  <!-- Sprint 65 S-ETS-65-01 (REQ-ETS-PART2-009): Part 2 JSON now implements the
       fourteen released Annex A procedures exactly. It still depends on "core common"
       rather than Part2ApiCommon, resource-class groups, or SystemFeatures so exact
       /conf/json declaration, the SWE JSON record-components prerequisite, resource
       condition gates, and public-IUT no-mutation behavior remain runtime-visible before
       JSON-specific resource endpoint access. -->
  <!-- Sprint 29 S-ETS-29-01 (REQ-ETS-PART2-010): Part 2 SWE Common JSON group
       added as a declaration-gated, read-only schema/media-validation subset. It
       depends on "core common" rather than Part2ApiCommon, resource-class groups, or
       SystemFeatures so exact /conf/swecommon-json declaration, SWE Encoding Rules
       prerequisite visibility, resource condition gates, and public-IUT no-mutation
       behavior remain runtime-visible. -->
  <!-- Sprint 30 S-ETS-30-01 (REQ-ETS-PART2-011): Part 2 SWE Common Text group
       added as a declaration-gated, read-only schema/media-validation subset. It
       depends on "core common" rather than Part2ApiCommon, resource-class groups, or
       SystemFeatures so exact /conf/swecommon-text declaration, SWE Text Encoding Rules
       prerequisite visibility, resource condition gates, exact application/swe+text
       evidence, and public-IUT no-mutation behavior remain runtime-visible. -->
  <!-- Sprint 31 S-ETS-31-01 (REQ-ETS-PART2-012): Part 2 SWE Common Binary group
       added as a declaration-gated, read-only schema/media-validation subset. It
       depends on "core common" rather than Part2ApiCommon, resource-class groups, or
       SystemFeatures so exact /conf/swecommon-binary declaration, SWE Binary Encoding
       Rules prerequisite visibility, resource condition gates, exact
       application/swe+binary evidence, and public-IUT no-mutation behavior remain
       runtime-visible. -->
  <!-- Sprint 32 S-ETS-32-01 (REQ-ETS-PART2-013): Part 2 Binding group added as an
       internal cross-class closure over OGC 23-002 Datastream/Observation and
       ControlStream/Command schema requirements. It deliberately does not advertise,
       depend on, or require a standalone /conf/observation-binding class because OGC
       23-002 defines no such conformance class. It depends on "core common" only so
       DataStream/ControlStream declarations, empty local OSH seed state, and encoding
       honesty remain runtime-visible. -->
  <test name="Conformance Classes - Core + SystemFeatures + Common + Subsystems + Procedures + Deployments + SamplingFeatures + PropertyDefinitions + Subdeployments + GeoJSON + SensorML + AdvancedFiltering + CreateReplaceDelete + Update + Part2ApiCommon + Part2Datastream + Part2ControlStream + Part2Feasibility + Part2SystemEvent + Part2AdvancedFiltering + Part2CreateReplaceDelete + Part2Update + Part2Json + Part2SweCommonJson + Part2SweCommonText + Part2SweCommonBinary + Part2Binding (OGC 23-001 /conf/core, /conf/system, /conf/subsystem, /conf/procedure, /conf/deployment, /conf/sf, /conf/property, /conf/subdeployment, /conf/geojson, /conf/sensorml, /conf/advanced-filtering, /conf/create-replace-delete, /conf/update; OGC 23-002 /conf/api-common, /conf/datastream, /conf/controlstream, /conf/feasibility, /conf/system-event, /conf/advanced-filtering, /conf/create-replace-delete, /conf/update, /conf/json, /conf/swecommon-json, /conf/swecommon-text, /conf/swecommon-binary; internal REQ-ETS-PART2-013 binding closure; OGC 19-072 /conf/common)">
    <groups>
      <dependencies>
        <group name="part1apicommon" depends-on="core common"/>
        <group name="systemfeatures" depends-on="part1apicommon"/>
        <group name="subsystems" depends-on="systemfeatures"/>
